course: dictionary
lesson: 15661
title: Thinness and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Thinness is a noun, made from the word thin. It names the state of being thin. Like many words, it can have more than one meaning, so use the words around it to choose the right one. «The thinness of the ice meant it could crack under our feet.» Here the ice is not thick, so it is dangerous.
explain: Thinness can also describe a person or animal. «The doctor was worried about the boy's thinness after weeks of illness.» Here thinness means having little fat on the body. The clue is illness, which can make a body lose weight.
explain: Thinness can also mean watery or weak, with not much in it. «The soup tasted of little more than hot water, and its thinness made it dull.» The clue is the word soup and the complaint that it tasted of little. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: Thinness is a noun, made from the adjective thin.
fact: «Thinness» can mean not thick, having little fat on the body, or being watery and weak.
fact: In science and maths, thinness is measured as thickness, in millimetres (mm).
fact: «The thinness of the ice» is a safety danger on ponds, so never walk on thin ice.
fact: Bodies come in many healthy shapes, and very great thinness can be a sign of illness. Nobody should be teased about their body.
exercise: «The thinness of the ice meant it could crack under our feet.» What does thinness mean here? | *Not thick, so it could break easily | Having lots of fat | Being very tall | Being very cold
exercise: «The soup had so little in it that its thinness was clear.» What does thinness mean in this sentence? | *Being watery, with not much in it | Being full to the top | Being thick and warm | Having lots of spices
exercise: In science, how is the thinness of a sheet of card measured? | *In millimetres | In kilograms | In hours | In litres
test: «The doctor was worried about the boy's extreme thinness after weeks of illness.» What can very great thinness sometimes be a sign of? | *Illness | Good luck | Being tall | Being happy
test: Which meaning fits thinness of a person? | Having lots of muscle | Being very loud | Being very old | *Having little fat on the body
exam: Why should nobody be teased about their body or their thinness? | Because only thin people are healthy | Because teasing makes people taller | *Because bodies come in many healthy shapes, and teasing hurts | Because teasing is good exercise
